{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["אמונה — firm, by their strength. And likewise: ״ותקעתיו יתד במקום נאמן״, a strong place. And likewise: ״בכל דור ודור אמונתו״, his endurance for generation after generation. And likewise: ״וחלים רעים ונאמנים״ — lasting illnesses, chronic and enduring ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The lemma אמונה in context (Exodus 17:12) describes Moses' hands as steady/firm; Rashbam supports this sense of ne'eman/emunah as 'firm, enduring' with four citations. The fourth example reads וחלים רעים ונאמנים as describing illnesses that are severe and entrenched, glossing with חלאים ארוכים וקיימים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:52.847666021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}